// A drive-in hot dog stand at the city's edge, its hero landmark: two giant franks standing on the
// roof (he in a vest, bow tie and boater, waving; she in a full skirt with a bow, arms out), their
// eyes lit red at night; two carhop canopies down the lot with a menu board and a speaker post at
// every stall; HOT DOGS in neon on the band and on a blade sign by the road. Roadside kitsch of
// the late 1940s, still open. Kit format: crates/world/src/landmarks.rs and
// docs/adr/0007-landmark-kits.md. Kit frame, m: x across the lot (to the right seen from the road),
// y up, z toward the road; the lot spans x -20..20 and z -46..0.
